  "summary": "Your messages queue is clear. I handled 7 refill messages for 3 patients under the refill protocol (RBC-RX-05). Three new results came in while I worked; they reversed two refills and upgraded a third, and I corrected all three. Two lisinopril refills are waiting for your review.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030)**\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0002). His kidney filtration rate (eGFR) is 58 after a lab correction. His HbA1c was 7.1% on an outside test from 08/19. There were 4 messages about metformin (his portal message and two pharmacy requests); I treated them as one request and placed one order.\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled.** I first renewed it, then a corrected result arrived: his 10/06 creatinine is 1.49, not 1.36. That is 35% above the 1.10 measured before you raised the dose on 09/18. The protocol treats a rise over 30% within 4 weeks like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled my order (mr-t0001) before anything was dispensed. A review task is with you (task-t0011, focus mr-00295). He says his 30-day supply has run out.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027)**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled.** The potassium of 5.9 on 08/27 doesn't count because the sample was hemolyzed. Using the last valid potassium (4.5, from January), I renewed it and ordered a repeat BMP. Then an outside BMP from 10/20 arrived on a good sample, with potassium 5.8. I cancelled my order (mr-t0003) before anything was dispensed. A review task is with you (task-t0012, focus mr-00283). His hernia repair has been moved to 11/12.\n- The BMP I ordered (sr-t0006) is still open; I can't cancel lab orders with my tools. Please decide whether he still needs it.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0005). I ignored the eGFR of 39 from 10/14 because it was marked entered in error; his valid eGFR is 90–92 and HbA1c was 6.9% on 09/28.\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0010). His last BMP was over 12 months old, so I first gave a 30-day supply and ordered a BMP. A BMP from 10/22 then arrived (potassium 4.6), so I replaced the short supply with the full renewal.\n- The BMP I ordered (sr-t0007) is now redundant, and I couldn't cancel it either.\n\nEach patient got a portal reply saying what was done, and I wrote a protocol note in each chart. I left the three new result items (inbox-a0001, a0003, a0004) open in your results queue so you can see them. I didn't touch the older items in your results queue, since they weren't part of this request.",
